| Attack                              | Category                   | What It Does                                                               | Main Resource/Target                      | Key Thing to Remember                     |
| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **UDP Flood**                       | Volumetric                 | Sends huge amounts of UDP traffic to a target                              | Bandwidth, network resources              | **Flood with UDP packets**                |
| **ICMP Flood**                      | Volumetric                 | Sends large amounts of ICMP traffic                                        | Bandwidth, CPU, network resources         | **Flood with ICMP traffic**               |
| **Ping Flood**                      | Volumetric                 | Sends massive numbers of ICMP Echo Requests                                | Network and system resources              | **Flood with ping requests**              |
| **DNS Amplification**               | Volumetric / Amplification | Uses DNS servers to generate larger responses toward the victim            | Bandwidth                                 | **Small request → large DNS response**    |
| **NTP Amplification**               | Volumetric / Amplification | Abuses NTP servers to amplify traffic toward the victim                    | Bandwidth                                 | **Small request → large NTP response**    |
| **Memcached Amplification**         | Volumetric / Amplification | Abuses exposed Memcached servers to generate very large responses          | Bandwidth                                 | **Small request → huge response**         |
| **SYN Flood**                       | Protocol                   | Sends many TCP SYN requests without completing the handshake               | TCP connection resources                  | **Exhaust incomplete connections**        |
| **Ping of Death**                   | Protocol                   | Sends malformed or oversized ICMP packets                                  | Vulnerable operating system               | **Malformed/oversized packets**           |
| **Teardrop**                        | Protocol                   | Sends malformed or overlapping IP fragments                                | Packet reassembly/system resources        | **Overlapping fragments**                 |
| **TCP Connection Exhaustion**       | Protocol                   | Attempts to consume available TCP connections                              | Connection tables/resources               | **Use up TCP connections**                |
| **HTTP Flood**                      | Application Layer          | Sends huge numbers of HTTP requests                                        | Web server/application                    | **Flood the web application**             |
| **Slowloris**                       | Application Layer          | Keeps many HTTP connections open by sending requests very slowly           | Web server connections                    | **Slow requests → connections stay open** |
| **Application Resource Exhaustion** | Application Layer          | Forces applications to perform resource-intensive operations               | CPU, RAM, database, application resources | **Make the application waste resources**  |
| **Zero-Day DoS**                    | Varies                     | Exploits an unknown or unpatched vulnerability to cause service disruption | Depends on vulnerability                  | **Unknown/unpatched vulnerability**       |
| **DDoS**                            | Distributed                | Uses many systems to attack a target simultaneously                        | Network/server/application resources      | **Many sources → one target**             |
